== 6.8 Chapter 6 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [A pest is best defined as any organism that],
  [is an insect],
  [reduces the quantity or quality of what the farmer produces],
  [lives on the farm],
  [feeds on other insects]
)

#mcq(2, [An insect with piercing and sucking mouthparts],
  [removes sap and causes yellowing and distortion],
  [chews holes in the leaves],
  [cuts the stem at the base],
  [bores into the fruit]
)

#mcq(3, [The insecticide most effective against a sucking insect is one that is],
  [a contact dust],
  [a stomach poison],
  [a seed dressing],
  [systemic]
)

#mcq(4, [A biting and chewing insect is best controlled with],
  [a stomach poison taken in with the leaf],
  [a systemic only],
  [a soil fumigant],
  [a nematicide]
)

#mcq(5, [The maize stem borer damages the crop by],
  [eating the roots only],
  [sucking sap from the leaf],
  [tunnelling inside the stem],
  [attacking the stored grain]
)

#mcq(6, [The cowpea weevil is chiefly a],
  [field pest of the seedling],
  [root pest],
  [leaf pest],
  [storage pest of the dried seed]
)

#mcq(7, [The variegated grasshopper damages cassava by],
  [boring the stem],
  [attacking the roots],
  [sucking the sap],
  [eating the leaves]
)

#mcq(8, [Root-knot nematodes are recognised by],
  [white mould on the pods],
  [galls on the roots],
  [mosaic on the leaves],
  [holes in the leaves]
)

#mcq(9, [Quelea birds are a serious pest of],
  [cassava roots],
  [stored yams],
  [ripening rice and sorghum],
  [cocoa pods]
)

#mcq(10, [Black pod disease of cocoa is caused by a],
  [fungus],
  [virus],
  [bacterium],
  [nematode]
)

#mcq(11, [A disease showing mosaic patterns and mottling on the leaves with no mould is most likely],
  [viral],
  [nutritional],
  [bacterial],
  [fungal]
)

#mcq(12, [Bacterial diseases are often recognised by],
  [water-soaked spots and wilts, sometimes with a yellow halo],
  [hollow stems],
  [white powdery growth],
  [grey flecks]
)

#mcq(13, [Cassava mosaic disease is spread mainly by],
  [wind],
  [seed],
  [whiteflies],
  [nematodes]
)

#mcq(14, [Damping-off in a nursery is controlled chiefly by],
  [sterilising the medium and using clean seed],
  [adding more shade],
  [watering more often],
  [sowing more densely]
)

#mcq(15, [The disease triangle consists of the host, the pathogen and],
  [a favourable environment],
  [a vector],
  [a weed],
  [a fertiliser]
)

#mcq(16, [A weed is best defined as],
  [a plant growing where it is not wanted],
  [a plant with a deep root],
  [a plant that is poisonous],
  [any plant that is not a crop]
)

#mcq(17, [*Striga* is serious because it is],
  [a storage mould],
  [an insect that attacks roots],
  [a competitor for light only],
  [a parasite that draws food from the roots of cereals]
)

#mcq(18, [Spear grass is difficult to control because it],
  [is eaten by cattle only],
  [is an annual with no seed],
  [grows only in water],
  [has deep rhizomes that survive hoeing and burning]
)

#mcq(19, [Water hyacinth is a problem mainly because it],
  [dries out the river],
  [blocks waterways and interferes with fishing],
  [poisons the fish],
  [attacks the rice plant]
)

#mcq(20, [Which of these is a cultural method of weed control?],
  [releasing an insect enemy],
  [spraying glyphosate],
  [smothering weeds with a close-planted cover crop],
  [hand pulling]
)

#mcq(21, [A selective herbicide is one that],
  [is applied only to the seed],
  [kills every plant it touches],
  [works only in the soil],
  [kills certain weeds without killing the crop]
)

#mcq(22, [Biological control of a weed works by],
  [spraying a herbicide],
  [introducing a natural enemy of the weed],
  [planting a cover crop],
  [ploughing the field]
)

#mcq(23, [Integrated pest management means],
  [spraying weekly],
  [combining cultural, biological, genetic and chemical methods],
  [using only resistant varieties],
  [abandoning chemicals altogether]
)

#mcq(24, [The pre-harvest interval printed on a pesticide label is the],
  [time the crop takes to mature],
  [interval between two sprays],
  [time that must pass between spraying and harvesting],
  [time the chemical stays in the shop]
)

#mcq(25, [A wettable powder is a pesticide formulation that],
  [is applied as granules],
  [is applied as a dust],
  [forms a suspension when mixed with water],
  [dissolves completely in water]
)

#mcq(26, [Crop rotation controls soil-borne pests because],
  [it raises the pH],
  [it kills the pest with chemicals],
  [it floods the field],
  [the pest cannot find its host when the crop changes]
)

#mcq(27, [Destroying crop refuse after harvest is a control measure against],
  [pests and diseases that overwinter in the trash],
  [nematodes only],
  [birds only],
  [weeds only]
)

#mcq(28, [Resistant varieties control disease by],
  [increasing the plant population],
  [preventing the pathogen from establishing in the plant],
  [raising the soil pH],
  [killing the vector]
)

#mcq(29, [Which of these is a biting and chewing pest?],
  [whitefly],
  [caterpillar],
  [thrips],
  [aphid]
)

#mcq(30, [The cassava mealybug damages the crop by],
  [attacking the seed],
  [eating the root],
  [boring into the tuber],
  [sucking sap and distorting the growing shoot]
)

#mcq(31, [Which of these practices would increase a pest problem rather than reduce it?],
  [growing the same crop on the same land every year],
  [rotating with a non-host crop],
  [planting resistant varieties],
  [destroying crop residue]
)

#mcq(32, [The correct protective clothing for spraying includes],
  [no protection if the chemical is dilute],
  [overall, gloves, boots and a face mask],
  [sandals and shorts],
  [a hat only]
)

#mcq(33, [A fungicide is used against],
  [nematodes],
  [insects],
  [fungal diseases such as blights and mildews],
  [weeds]
)

#mcq(34, [Weeds reduce crop yield mainly by],
  [shading the soil beneficially],
  [competing for water, light and nutrients],
  [adding organic matter],
  [fixing nitrogen]
)

#mcq(35, [Which of these is a preventive rather than a curative weed control measure?],
  [hoeing the established weeds],
  [spraying a contact herbicide],
  [pulling weeds by hand],
  [using clean seed and clean implements]
)

#mcq(36, [Nematodes are controlled most effectively by],
  [adding urea to the surface],
  [spraying the leaves],
  [crop rotation with a non-host and resistant varieties],
  [burning the crop residue]
)

#mcq(37, [A virus disease is difficult to control directly because],
  [there is no chemical that kills a virus inside a plant],
  [it only affects the roots],
  [it cannot be transmitted],
  [it is caused by a fungus]
)

#mcq(38, [The economic threshold in pest management is the],
  [maximum legal dose of a pesticide],
  [pest population at which control becomes worth the cost],
  [number of sprays allowed per season],
  [price of the pesticide]
)

#mcq(39, [Which of these is a mollusc pest of seedlings?],
  [weevil],
  [aphid],
  [nematode],
  [snail]
)

#mcq(40, [Herbicides are classified as],
  [insecticides],
  [fertilisers],
  [fungicides],
  [pesticides that kill weeds]
)

